@handlewithcare/react-prosemirror, FlightSpec fork

This package is a modified version of @handlewithcare/react-prosemirror 3.2.5
(https://github.com/handlewithcarecollective/react-prosemirror, tag v3.2.5),
Copyright (c) 2025 Handle with Care Collective, licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE.txt).

The modifications live on the `flightspec` branch of
https://github.com/wizzboy55/react-prosemirror, one commit per change, so each
can be upstreamed or dropped on its own. They were made for the FlightSpec
document editor in 2026 and are distributed under the same license.

Modifications:

- Packaging: build on install from a git dependency (`prepare` script), an npm
  lockfile for that build, and this NOTICE.
  Files: package.json, package-lock.json, NOTICE.

- Render and commit once per transaction: DocNodeView's imperative handles
  take deps (no setMount(null)/setMount(el) per render), and LayoutGroup no
  longer forces a re-render for effects registered in a commit that already
  runs its layout effect.
  Files: src/components/nodes/DocNodeView.tsx, src/components/LayoutGroup.tsx,
  src/components/__tests__/renderPasses.test.tsx.

- Stable context above the node views: ProseMirrorInner publishes the editor
  state and the doc node view props through a stable store instead of
  per-transaction context values; useEditorState and ProseMirrorDoc render in
  the dispatch's pass, EditorStateContext is removed, and the node view
  component maps keep their context value while shallowly equal.
  Files: src/components/ProseMirror.tsx, src/components/ProseMirrorDoc.tsx,
  src/components/EditorStateSelectorsProvider.tsx,
  src/contexts/EditorStateStoreContext.ts, src/contexts/EditorStateContext.ts
  (removed), src/hooks/useEditor.ts, src/hooks/useEditorState.ts,
  src/hooks/useEditorStoreConsumer.ts,
  src/hooks/__tests__/useEditorEffect.test.tsx,
  src/components/__tests__/renderPasses.test.tsx.

- No per-node store subscription: the editor store computes the composition
  freeze position once per state and notifies node views only when it
  changes, instead of every NodeView running a getPos() selector per state.
  Files: src/contexts/EditorStateStoreContext.ts,
  src/components/nodes/NodeView.tsx,
  src/components/__tests__/renderPasses.test.tsx.

- Incremental reactKeys: keys live in a persistent position-sorted index, so a
  transaction remaps only the entries inside its changed range and keys only
  the node starts that range introduced (identical keys to the full remap);
  posToKey/keyToPos are built on first read and keyAt() reads one key.
  reactKeys({ keysFrom }) carries keys across a whole-state replacement by
  pairing the old and new documents, so unchanged nodes are not remounted.
  Files: src/plugins/reactKeys.ts, src/plugins/keyIndex.ts (new),
  src/components/ChildNodeViews.tsx,
  src/plugins/__tests__/reactKeys.incremental.test.ts (new).

- Single-pass mount: the editor renders its first pass against a provisional
  static view that resolves node views and `editable` like the mounted view,
  and creates the ReactEditorView in the document root's ref during that
  commit. Node and mark views build their descriptions in the same commit, in
  layout-effect order, and editor effects run once with the mounted view. The
  editor context value keeps its identity when the view mounts (the view is
  read when used), DOM event registration no longer changes it, the view is
  updated only when its props change, and a React node view assumes a content
  DOM for a node with content on its first render instead of rendering again
  once it mounts. Prop DOM event handlers run after component handlers.
  Files: src/hooks/useEditor.ts, src/components/ProseMirror.tsx,
  src/StaticEditorView.ts, src/ReactEditorView.ts, src/AbstractEditorView.ts,
  src/contexts/EditorContext.ts, src/hooks/useNodeViewDescription.ts,
  src/hooks/useMarkViewDescription.ts, src/hooks/useEditorEffect.ts,
  src/hooks/useEditorEventCallback.ts, src/hooks/useComponentEventListeners.tsx,
  src/hooks/useReactKeys.ts, src/components/TextNodeView.tsx,
  src/components/ChildNodeViews.tsx, src/components/SeparatorHackView.tsx,
  src/components/nodes/ReactNodeView.tsx, src/decorations/computeDocDeco.ts,
  src/decorations/viewDecorations.tsx,
  src/tiptap/hooks/useTiptapEditorEffect.ts,
  src/hooks/__tests__/useEditorEffect.test.tsx,
  src/components/__tests__/renderPasses.test.tsx.

- Fewer fibers per node and an ordered child build: NodeView keys its node
  view by the remount count and by the component or constructor, replacing
  RemountableNodeView and the per-type wrapper component; one provider
  carries a node view's select, stop-event and ignore-mutation handlers (a
  mark view passes them on with its own ignore-mutation handler), replacing
  three; text node views read the child descriptions context directly.
  ChildNodeViews builds its children in document order instead of sorting
  them, falling back to the sort only when a key repeats, and reads the node
  keys once per child list.
  Files: src/components/nodes/NodeView.tsx,
  src/components/nodes/ReactNodeView.tsx,
  src/components/marks/ReactMarkView.tsx, src/components/ChildNodeViews.tsx,
  src/contexts/NodeViewHandlersContext.ts (new),
  src/contexts/SelectNodeContext.ts, src/contexts/StopEventContext.ts and
  src/contexts/IgnoreMutationContext.ts (removed), src/hooks/useSelectNode.ts,
  src/hooks/useStopEvent.ts, src/hooks/useIgnoreMutation.ts,
  src/components/__tests__/renderPasses.test.tsx.
